    "info(c) = uint256(chain_id) ‖ entry_point ‖ vault ‖ factory ‖ paymaster ‖ keccak256(account_creation_code) ‖ payee ‖ uint32(c): big-endian, addresses 20 bytes, 168 bytes",
    "k(c) = HKDF-Expand(SHA-256, PRK, info(c), 32) as a big-endian integer; the owner key is k(c) for the first c = 0, 1, ... with 1 <= k(c) <= n - 1 (secp256k1)",
    "transit_account = CREATE2(factory, salt 0, keccak256(account_creation_code ‖ abi.encode(entry_point, vault, paymaster, owner, payee)))",
    "reject_counters: the test replaces the expansion at these counters with an invalid scalar (n, then 0, alternating), so the derivation resamples; owner_private_key is k(counter)"
